Package: gmediation
Type: Package
Title: Mediation Analysis for Multiple and Multi-Stage Mediators
Version: 2.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jang Ik", "Cho", email = "jxc864@case.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Jeffrey", "Albert", role = "aut"))
Description: Conducts causal mediation and path analysis for multiple
    mediators arranged in up to two stages. The function gmediate() estimates
    individual path effects, first- and second-stage mediator effects, and
    the total exposure effect, together with bootstrap confidence intervals,
    for models fit by the user for the outcome and for each mediator. The
    function gmedsens() extends this to a probabilistic sensitivity analysis
    that evaluates the robustness of path effect estimates to a range of
    assumed correlations between residuals of non-identifiable paths. Both
    functions default to using the entire (complete case) sample as the
    reference group unless a different reference group is specified.
